  Execution decisions (2026-11-05; implemented, qualified and accepted)
    AO horizon: retain the existing case-owned ComponentShaderPrograms lifetime and create one
    four-program bundle per case, borrowing it from fresh scene fixtures. Rebind changing inputs
    and clear borrowed sampler/camera references before scene resources retire. The 236 -> 40
    creation count applies to ten correctness cases; diagnostic cases remain separately selected.
    Surface-work collection: specialize the bounded collector case with a real precompiled compute
    submission and the production collector, preserving fences, readback, capacity, independent
    snapshots and disposal. CPU-written counters cannot replace its compute submission boundary.
    Preserve ConsumerRuntime and SpatialRuntime owners and publication chains. Water composition
    and direct-visibility owners also remain unchanged unless a bounded complete reset design is
    established; their API/asset, variant and mutable resource lifetimes exceed the existing seam.
    Atmosphere reductions approved by the user on 2026-11-05 (qualified):
      Keep all current cases. GroundAlbedoInvalidatesCpuTransport retains its real synchronous
      .1/.8 numerical integrations; controlled completions replace its two worker integrations,
      asserting exact admitted requests, publication identity and .801 bucket reuse. The independent
      real-worker PublishesOnlyCompletedSnapshotAndReusesStableInputs witness remains unchanged.
      RefreshNeverPublishesPartialResults and StableQuantizedInputsDoNotRefresh use 17x9 grids
      (153 samples, two 128-sample update intervals with a 25-sample tail) instead of 32x24/768.
      ChangingInputsFinishAdmittedSnapshotThenRefreshLatest uses 20x20/400 (four intervals), retaining
      two changed requests during the pending build. Both resize methods use old 17x9 -> new 16x9,
      retaining distinct dimensions, both pending/publication states and independent full expected
      snapshots. WeatherRefreshStillPublishesOnlyAfterPartialFinalBatch and the timing diagnostic
      remain unchanged. Default-size real construction remains in CancelledLookupPreservesPreviousSnapshot;
      explicit 33x25 and 128x96 complete dimension witnesses and quality mapping remain unchanged.
